+2026-10-05 Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
+
+	Popover shadows: menus get libadwaita's popover shadow round their
+	rounded corners, in a transparent margin as windows do.
+	* Source/x11/XGServerWindow.m (popoverMargin, marginFor): New.  A
+	popover's margin, smaller than a window's.
+	(-_windowGetsPopoverShadow:): New.  A borderless window marked with
+	NSUtilityWindowMask (which a borderless window has no other use for;
+	a theme marks its menus) gets a popover's margin when
+	GSBackPopoverShadows is YES, on a window's terms: the gui draws the
+	decorations, the window manager lists _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS and the
+	compositing manager shows transparency.  GSBackPopoverCornerRadius
+	rounds its corners.
+	(-window::::, -_updateShadowSizeOf:): Use the window's margin.
+	* Source/cairo/XGCairoModernSurface.m (box_shadow_layer,
+	popover_shadow_alpha): New.  libadwaita's popover box-shadow, two
+	blurred layers, each from the distance to the popover's rounded
+	outline (grown by its spread), so it follows the rounded corners.
+	(shadow_template, create_shadow): Take the kind of shadow; keep a
+	template for each.
+	* Headers/x11/XGServerWindow.h: Add shadow_popover to
+	gswindow_device_t.
+	* Tests/x11/shadowmargin.m: Check popovers' margin and input shape.
+
+2026-10-05 Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
+
+	Window types as GTK sets them, so window managers neither focus nor
+	animate menus and tool tips, and compositors can key shadows and
+	fades on the type.
+	* Source/x11/XGServerWindow.m (-_setWindowType:): New, from
+	-setwindowlevel::.  A tool tip (GSTTPanel) is _TOOLTIP, a menu at
+	the pop-up menu level (a context menu or a pop-up button's) is
+	_POPUP_MENU rather than _DIALOG, a drag image is _DND, and a modal
+	panel is _DIALOG rather than _NORMAL.  The new types are followed by
+	_DIALOG, their old type, for window managers that don't know them
+	(Openbox).  Other windows keep their types.
+	(-setwindowlevel::): Use it.
+	(-orderwindow:::): Set the type again just before mapping a window
+	at the pop-up menu level: a tool tip's level is set before its window
+	is registered, so its class wasn't known and it was typed _DIALOG.
+	* Tests/x11/windowtype.m: New test.
+
+2026-10-02 Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
+
+	Window shadows, rounded corners and window manager functions for
+	windows whose decorations the gui draws (GSBackHandlesWindowDecorations
+	or GSX11HandlesWindowDecorations NO), as GTK's client-side
+	decorations have them under GNOME's Mutter.
+	* Source/x11/XGServerWindow.m (setWindowHintsForStyle): For a styled
+	window the gui decorates, ask for no decorations but keep the
+	functions the style allows, plus move.  With functions 0 window
+	managers such as Mutter refused to move, resize, maximize, minimize
+	or close the window, even when asked with _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE or
+	_NET_WM_STATE.
+	(argb_visual, -_compositorRuns, -_compositorShowsAlpha,
+	-_windowGetsShadow:): New.  A styled, buffered window the gui
+	decorates gets a transparent margin for a shadow when the
+	GSBackWindowShadows default is YES (a theme sets it in its
+	GSThemeDomain), the window manager lists _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS in
+	_NET_SUPPORTED and a compositing manager runs, with a 32-bit visual
+	of its own (one per screen).  GSBackWindowCornerRadius rounds its
+	corners.
+	(-_compositorChanged): New.  When the compositing manager stops,
+	windows lose their margin, which would show black; they get it back
+	when one starts.
+	(-_windowGetsAlpha:): New.  A borderless window (menus, tool tips)
+	gets the 32-bit visual when GSBackBorderlessWindowAlpha is YES and a
+	compositing manager runs, so what the gui leaves transparent, such
+	as rounded corners, shows what is behind it.
+	(-_offsets::::for:): New.  The offsets between the frame and the X
+	window: the window manager's decorations when it draws them, else
+	minus the shadow margin.  Use it in the frame, window rectangle and
+	point conversions, -setWindowdevice:forContext: and
+	-flushwindowrect::.
+	(-_updateShadowSizeOf:): New.  No margin while the window manager
+	has the window maximized, fullscreen or tiled (_NET_WM_STATE,
+	_GTK_EDGE_CONSTRAINTS) or no compositing manager runs; move the
+	minimum and maximum size hints with the margin.
+	(-_updateShadowOf:): New.  Set _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS to the margin, and
+	an input shape of the visible part and, for a resizable window, a
+	12 pixel band round it, which the gui uses to resize.
+	(shadowScale, shadowScaled): New.  The margin, the corner radius and
+	the resize band are in points: multiply them by the gui's scale
+	factor (GSScaleFactor), as GTK's grow with its scale.
+	(-window::::): Create such windows with the 32-bit visual, and the
+	margin where they have one.
+	(-placewindow::): Reshape the input region when the size changes:
+	the ConfigureNotify that follows finds xframe already updated.
+	* Source/x11/XGServerEvent.m: Use -_offsets::::for: for event
+	locations.  On ConfigureNotify reshape the input region; on Expose
+	copy the margin from the backing store; on PropertyNotify of
+	_NET_WM_STATE or _GTK_EDGE_CONSTRAINTS update the margin.
+	(-_shadowSizeChangedFor:, -_settleShadowOf:, -_shadowSettled:): New.
+	After the margin changed the window manager fits the X window to it,
+	usually configuring it for the old margin first: hold the frame from
+	the gui until the ConfigureNotify events stop (50 ms with none, 300 ms
+	at most), then send it once, so a maximize is one resize rather than
+	three, and expose the whole window from the buffers, which have the
+	margin now.  On ConfigureNotify also look for a margin change, as the
+	window manager may configure the window before the PropertyNotify for
+	its new state arrives.  On the XFixes selection event for
+	_NET_WM_CM_S<n>, call -_compositorChanged.
+	* Source/x11/XGServer.m: Watch the _NET_WM_CM_S<n> selection with
+	XFixes.
+	* Headers/x11/XGServer.h: Add xfixesEventBase.
+	* Source/x11/XGGLContext.m: Place an OpenGL view's X window with
+	-_offsets::::for:, so it is where the view is in a window with a
+	margin.
+	* Tests/x11/shadowmargin.m: New test, with a window manager and a
+	compositing manager of its own.
+	* Tests/x11/GNUmakefile: Add it.
+	* Source/cairo/XGCairoModernSurface.m (shadow_alpha, shadow_template,
+	create_shadow): New.  The shadow, as libadwaita's under Mutter, put
+	together in the X server from corners and edges computed once, its
+	fall-off scaled with the window's scale factor.
+	(-initWithDevice:): Make the shadow for a window with a margin.
+	(-handleExposeRect:): Copy the window's contents and the shadow as
+	rectangles, and the four corners through a rounded clip.
+	* Headers/cairo/XGCairoModernSurface.h: Add _shadowSurface.
+	* Headers/x11/XGServerWindow.h: Add shadow, corner_radius,
+	shadow_scale, shadow_eligible, shadow_resizable, shadow_settling and
+	shadow_settle_start to gswindow_device_t.  Declare -_offsets::::for:,
+	-_updateShadowOf:, -_updateShadowSizeOf:, -_shadowSizeChangedFor:,
+	-_shadowSettled:, -_compositorRuns and -_compositorChanged.
+	* Headers/x11/XGGeneric.h: Add the _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS and
+	_GTK_EDGE_CONSTRAINTS atoms.
+
